<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bad Ems</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bad Ems is a spa town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the river <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahn">Lahn</a>. Its warm springs made it one of the most fashionable resorts of 19th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, visited by royalty. It is best known for the Ems Dispatch of July 1870, Bismarck's edited report of King William I's meeting there with the French ambassador, which helped provoke the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-prussian-war">Franco-Prussian War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bad-ems.jpg" alt="Bad Ems" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julian Lupyan · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buildings_in_Bad_Ems,_Germany.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
